# ============================================================
# SEMANTICSCRIPT STANDARD LIBRARY: native bcrypt namespace
# ============================================================
#
# Import this module with:
#
#   import bcrypt standard.bcrypt
#
# The `bcrypt.*` call targets are compiler/runtime-owned intrinsics
# backed by the vendored crypt_blowfish 1.3 implementation at
# `third_party/bcrypt/` plus the platform CSPRNG (BCryptGenRandom on
# Windows, getrandom on Linux, /dev/urandom fallback). This module owns
# the official standard-library import path and the trust-type
# contracts for that intrinsic namespace.

# rationale: Standard-library namespace and trust contracts for password hashing (bcrypt $2b$ with caller-chosen cost), cryptographic randomness, and base64url encoding intrinsics.
# invariant: The standard module entry is this file; downstream modules may import it as alias `bcrypt` before using compiler-owned targets in the `bcrypt.*` namespace.
# security: BcryptPasswordHash values MUST always carry the `$2b$NN$...` prefix and exactly 60 chars; the native runtime adapter refuses to verify against any other format so a deployment cannot silently drift to a weaker variant by writing legacy `$2a$`/`$2x$`/`$2y$` strings to the database.
module standard.bcrypt
purpose module standard.bcrypt "Standard-library namespace and trust contracts for password hashing (bcrypt $2b$ with caller-chosen cost), cryptographic randomness, and base64url encoding intrinsics."
moduleOwns standard.bcrypt "The official import path `standard.bcrypt`, the BcryptPasswordHash / BcryptPlaintextPassword / SessionToken / CsrfToken trust types, the recommended cost-factor default, the session-token and CSRF-token byte-count defaults, and the required-output-buffer-size constants for hash + base64url."
moduleDoesNotOwn standard.bcrypt "The bcrypt algorithm implementation (crypt_blowfish.c lives under third_party/bcrypt/), the native CSPRNG (platform-specific entries in sem_bcrypt_runtime.c), caller-owned scratch-buffer allocation (apps must c.malloc the buffers themselves and defer c.free), or user-facing session storage (apps own the sessions SQL table)."
invariant module standard.bcrypt "The standard module entry is this file; downstream modules may import it as alias `bcrypt` before using compiler-owned targets in the `bcrypt.*` namespace."
moduleSecurity standard.bcrypt "BcryptPasswordHash values MUST always carry the `$2b$NN$...` prefix and exactly 60 chars; the native runtime adapter refuses to verify against any other format so a deployment cannot silently drift to a weaker variant by writing legacy `$2a$`/`$2x$`/`$2y$` strings to the database."
moduleSecurity standard.bcrypt "Authentication flows SHOULD keep bcrypt cost as an immutable source constant, use bcryptRecommendedCost unless the application policy chooses otherwise, and equalize public verification paths in `.sem` with a dummy bcrypt.verifyPassword when user-existence timing would leak account state. The compiler only lowers bcrypt.* ABI calls."
moduleSecurity standard.bcrypt "Prefer the Result-shaped targets (`bcrypt.hashPasswordResult`, `bcrypt.verifyPasswordResult`, `bcrypt.randomBytesResult`, `bcrypt.base64UrlEncodeResult`) when caller flow uses bind ok / bind error; raw status targets remain for low-level interop."
moduleSecurity standard.bcrypt "Persistent sessions SHOULD store only SessionTokenHash values produced by bcrypt.hashSessionTokenResult; compare presented SessionToken values with bcrypt.verifySessionTokenResult and never persist the raw token."
moduleSecurity standard.bcrypt "Session and CSRF tokens SHOULD be issued with bcrypt.issueSessionToken / bcrypt.issueCsrfToken or, when writing the primitive pattern manually, bcrypt.randomBytes followed by bcrypt.base64UrlEncode. Both one-step helpers are native-linkable in native and webServer builds."

# ----- trust types -----

type BcryptPlaintextPassword String
type BcryptPasswordHash String
type BcryptHashBuffer OpaquePointer
type BcryptRandomBuffer OpaquePointer
type SessionToken String
type SessionTokenHash String
type SessionTokenBuffer OpaquePointer
type CsrfToken String
type CsrfTokenBuffer OpaquePointer
type Base64UrlBuffer OpaquePointer

exportType standard.bcrypt BcryptPlaintextPassword
exportType standard.bcrypt BcryptPasswordHash
exportType standard.bcrypt BcryptHashBuffer
exportType standard.bcrypt BcryptRandomBuffer
exportType standard.bcrypt SessionToken
exportType standard.bcrypt SessionTokenHash
exportType standard.bcrypt SessionTokenBuffer
exportType standard.bcrypt CsrfToken
exportType standard.bcrypt CsrfTokenBuffer
exportType standard.bcrypt Base64UrlBuffer

typeInvariant BcryptPlaintextPassword "Untrusted user input. String-backed role alias at bcrypt argument sites: declare literals as String when module-scope role-alias constants do not lower, then pass the value to a BcryptPlaintextPassword argument row. Must NEVER be written to persistent storage."
typeTrust BcryptPlaintextPassword untrusted

typeInvariant BcryptPasswordHash "String-backed trusted role alias at bcrypt.verifyPassword argument sites. Exactly 60 characters with the `$2b$NN$...` prefix (cost NN in [4,31]). A successful BcryptHashBuffer is also a null-terminated hash string while the buffer remains live. Storage CHECK constraints in app SQL should enforce length(password_hash) = 60."
typeTrust BcryptPasswordHash trusted

typeInvariant BcryptHashBuffer "OpaquePointer-backed role alias at bcrypt.hashPassword argument sites. Caller-owned byte buffer with at least bcryptHashBufferRequiredBytes (61) bytes of capacity for the output; smaller buffers are rejected with SS_BCRYPT_ERR_CONFIG. Keep it live until all BcryptPasswordHash/String reads are complete, then release with c.free or memory.releaseMemoryBytes."
typeInvariant BcryptRandomBuffer "Caller-owned byte buffer of arbitrary capacity. Filled by bcrypt.randomBytes with platform-CSPRNG bytes; caller must c.free the buffer when done."
typeInvariant SessionToken "URL-safe opaque session identifier (43-char base64url, no padding). Always issued by encoding bcrypt.randomBytes output through bcrypt.base64UrlEncode — never derived from user input or any predictable source."
typeTrust SessionToken trusted

typeInvariant SessionTokenHash "String-backed at-rest session-token verifier. Store this value instead of the raw SessionToken; produce it with bcrypt.hashSessionTokenResult and verify presented tokens with bcrypt.verifySessionTokenResult."
typeTrust SessionTokenHash trusted

typeInvariant SessionTokenBuffer "Caller-owned byte buffer of at least sessionTokenBufferRequiredBytes (44) bytes capacity — the 43-char base64url payload plus the null terminator."
typeInvariant CsrfToken "URL-safe opaque anti-CSRF nonce (43-char base64url, no padding). Issue with bcrypt.issueCsrfToken, store server-side or in an integrity-protected session, embed in forms, and compare submitted values with text.equals."
typeTrust CsrfToken trusted

typeInvariant CsrfTokenBuffer "Caller-owned byte buffer of at least csrfTokenBufferRequiredBytes (44) bytes capacity — the 43-char base64url payload plus the null terminator."
typeInvariant Base64UrlBuffer "Caller-owned byte buffer for base64url output. Required capacity is ((inputBytes * 4) + 2) / 3 + 1 bytes — see bcrypt.base64UrlEncode for the rounding rule."

# ----- recommended defaults -----

storage module immutable bcryptModuleVersionText String "standard.bcrypt 0.1"

# Production cost factor: ~250ms per hash on a typical 2026 server CPU.
# Increase to 13-14 for a higher security margin if the registration /
# login latency budget can absorb 0.5s+ per hash.
storage module immutable bcryptRecommendedCost Int32 12

# Lower bound on the bcrypt format itself; below this the work factor
# is so small that brute-forcing is trivial.
storage module immutable bcryptMinimumCost Int32 4

# Format ceiling. Cost 31 takes ~16 hours per hash on modern CPUs and
# is impractical for interactive auth — listed only so apps can refuse
# nonsensical caller-supplied values upfront.
storage module immutable bcryptMaximumCost Int32 31

# Output-buffer sizes the native runtime requires. Apps that hash
# passwords must allocate a buffer of at least this many bytes; the
# native adapter rejects undersized buffers with SS_BCRYPT_ERR_CONFIG.
storage module immutable bcryptHashBufferRequiredBytes Int32 61

# Recommended session-token entropy: 32 bytes (256 bits) of CSPRNG
# output, base64url-encoded to a 43-char string + null terminator.
storage module immutable sessionTokenEntropyByteCount Int32 32
storage module immutable sessionTokenBufferRequiredBytes Int32 44
storage module immutable csrfTokenEntropyByteCount Int32 32
storage module immutable csrfTokenBufferRequiredBytes Int32 44

exportConstant standard.bcrypt bcryptModuleVersionText
exportConstant standard.bcrypt bcryptRecommendedCost
exportConstant standard.bcrypt bcryptMinimumCost
exportConstant standard.bcrypt bcryptMaximumCost
exportConstant standard.bcrypt bcryptHashBufferRequiredBytes
exportConstant standard.bcrypt sessionTokenEntropyByteCount
exportConstant standard.bcrypt sessionTokenBufferRequiredBytes
exportConstant standard.bcrypt csrfTokenEntropyByteCount
exportConstant standard.bcrypt csrfTokenBufferRequiredBytes

exportOperation standard.bcrypt hashPassword
exportOperation standard.bcrypt hashPasswordResult
exportOperation standard.bcrypt hashSessionTokenResult
exportOperation standard.bcrypt verifyPassword
exportOperation standard.bcrypt verifyPasswordResult
exportOperation standard.bcrypt verifySessionTokenResult
exportOperation standard.bcrypt randomBytes
exportOperation standard.bcrypt randomBytesResult
exportOperation standard.bcrypt base64UrlEncode
exportOperation standard.bcrypt base64UrlEncodeResult
exportOperation standard.bcrypt issueSessionToken
exportOperation standard.bcrypt issueCsrfToken

# rationale: Issue a fresh URL-safe session token by composing the two CSPRNG
#   primitives apps previously wired by hand. Field experience shows callers
#   misusing the manual path (e.g. hashing an email as a "token"); this gives
#   one correct call from raw entropy to a 43-char base64url SessionToken.
# invariant: On success returns 0; tokenBuffer holds a null-terminated 43-char
#   base64url token and tokenLengthOut receives its length. randomScratch needs
#   >= sessionTokenEntropyByteCount (32) bytes; tokenBuffer needs
#   >= sessionTokenBufferRequiredBytes (44) bytes.
# security: All token entropy comes from bcrypt.randomBytes (platform CSPRNG);
#   never derive a session token from user input or any predictable source.
operation issueSessionToken
input operation issueSessionToken randomScratch BcryptRandomBuffer
input operation issueSessionToken tokenBuffer Base64UrlBuffer
input operation issueSessionToken tokenCapacity Int32
input operation issueSessionToken tokenLengthOut OpaquePointer
output operation issueSessionToken Int32
effect issueSessionToken read system.random
effect issueSessionToken write memory.buffer
effect issueSessionToken read memory.buffer
authority issueSessionToken read system.random
authority issueSessionToken write memory.buffer
authority issueSessionToken read memory.buffer
memory issueSessionToken heap no
async issueSessionToken no
purpose operation issueSessionToken "Compose bcrypt.randomBytes + bcrypt.base64UrlEncode into one call that fills tokenBuffer with a fresh 43-char base64url session token."
invariant operation issueSessionToken "On success returns 0 and tokenBuffer holds a null-terminated 43-char base64url token; randomScratch must be >= sessionTokenEntropyByteCount bytes and tokenBuffer >= sessionTokenBufferRequiredBytes bytes."
security issueSessionToken "Token entropy comes only from bcrypt.randomBytes (platform CSPRNG); never derive a session token from user input or a predictable source."
failure issueSessionToken TokenIssueFailed "Returns a negative Int32 status when randomScratch is null/undersized, tokenBuffer or tokenLengthOut is invalid, tokenCapacity is below sessionTokenBufferRequiredBytes, or the platform CSPRNG fails."
label startIssueSessionToken
call sessionTokenRandomCall bcrypt.randomBytes
argument sessionTokenRandomCall outBuffer BcryptRandomBuffer randomScratch
argument sessionTokenRandomCall byteCount Int32 sessionTokenEntropyByteCount
run sessionTokenRandomCall
bind value sessionTokenRandomStatus Int32 sessionTokenRandomCall
storage local immutable sessionTokenStatusOk Int32 0
call sessionTokenRandomOkCall math.equalInt32
argument sessionTokenRandomOkCall left Int32 sessionTokenRandomStatus
argument sessionTokenRandomOkCall right Int32 sessionTokenStatusOk
run sessionTokenRandomOkCall
bind value sessionTokenRandomOk Bool sessionTokenRandomOkCall
branch if condition sessionTokenRandomOk target sessionTokenEncodeStep
return value sessionTokenRandomStatus
label sessionTokenEncodeStep
call sessionTokenEncodeCall bcrypt.base64UrlEncode
argument sessionTokenEncodeCall inputBuffer BcryptRandomBuffer randomScratch
argument sessionTokenEncodeCall inputCount Int32 sessionTokenEntropyByteCount
argument sessionTokenEncodeCall outputBuffer Base64UrlBuffer tokenBuffer
argument sessionTokenEncodeCall outputCapacity Int32 tokenCapacity
argument sessionTokenEncodeCall outputLengthOut OpaquePointer tokenLengthOut
run sessionTokenEncodeCall
bind value sessionTokenEncodeStatus Int32 sessionTokenEncodeCall
return value sessionTokenEncodeStatus

# rationale: Issue a fresh URL-safe CSRF token by composing CSPRNG bytes with
#   base64url encoding. The token shape matches session-token entropy but is a
#   separate semantic role so form tokens do not get confused with login
#   bearer/session credentials.
# invariant: On success returns 0; tokenBuffer holds a null-terminated 43-char
#   base64url token and tokenLengthOut receives its length. randomScratch needs
#   >= csrfTokenEntropyByteCount (32) bytes; tokenBuffer needs
#   >= csrfTokenBufferRequiredBytes (44) bytes.
# security: Store the issued value server-side or inside an integrity-protected
#   session, embed it in the form, and compare the submitted token with
#   text.equals before mutating requests.
operation issueCsrfToken
input operation issueCsrfToken randomScratch BcryptRandomBuffer
input operation issueCsrfToken tokenBuffer CsrfTokenBuffer
input operation issueCsrfToken tokenCapacity Int32
input operation issueCsrfToken tokenLengthOut OpaquePointer
output operation issueCsrfToken Int32
effect issueCsrfToken read system.random
effect issueCsrfToken write memory.buffer
effect issueCsrfToken read memory.buffer
authority issueCsrfToken read system.random
authority issueCsrfToken write memory.buffer
authority issueCsrfToken read memory.buffer
memory issueCsrfToken heap no
async issueCsrfToken no
purpose operation issueCsrfToken "Compose bcrypt.randomBytes + bcrypt.base64UrlEncode into one call that fills tokenBuffer with a fresh 43-char base64url CSRF token."
invariant operation issueCsrfToken "On success returns 0 and tokenBuffer holds a null-terminated 43-char base64url token; randomScratch must be >= csrfTokenEntropyByteCount bytes and tokenBuffer >= csrfTokenBufferRequiredBytes bytes."
security issueCsrfToken "CSRF token entropy comes only from bcrypt.randomBytes (platform CSPRNG); compare submitted form values with text.equals before mutating requests."
failure issueCsrfToken TokenIssueFailed "Returns a negative Int32 status when randomScratch is null/undersized, tokenBuffer or tokenLengthOut is invalid, tokenCapacity is below csrfTokenBufferRequiredBytes, or the platform CSPRNG fails."
label startIssueCsrfToken
call csrfTokenRandomCall bcrypt.randomBytes
argument csrfTokenRandomCall outBuffer BcryptRandomBuffer randomScratch
argument csrfTokenRandomCall byteCount Int32 csrfTokenEntropyByteCount
run csrfTokenRandomCall
bind value csrfTokenRandomStatus Int32 csrfTokenRandomCall
storage local immutable csrfTokenStatusOk Int32 0
call csrfTokenRandomOkCall math.equalInt32
argument csrfTokenRandomOkCall left Int32 csrfTokenRandomStatus
argument csrfTokenRandomOkCall right Int32 csrfTokenStatusOk
run csrfTokenRandomOkCall
bind value csrfTokenRandomOk Bool csrfTokenRandomOkCall
branch if condition csrfTokenRandomOk target csrfTokenEncodeStep
return value csrfTokenRandomStatus
label csrfTokenEncodeStep
call csrfTokenEncodeCall bcrypt.base64UrlEncode
argument csrfTokenEncodeCall inputBuffer BcryptRandomBuffer randomScratch
argument csrfTokenEncodeCall inputCount Int32 csrfTokenEntropyByteCount
argument csrfTokenEncodeCall outputBuffer Base64UrlBuffer tokenBuffer
argument csrfTokenEncodeCall outputCapacity Int32 tokenCapacity
argument csrfTokenEncodeCall outputLengthOut OpaquePointer tokenLengthOut
run csrfTokenEncodeCall
bind value csrfTokenEncodeStatus Int32 csrfTokenEncodeCall
return value csrfTokenEncodeStatus
